.Dd November 22, 2026
.Dt CUDA-NATIVE-TOOLCHAIN 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cuda-native-toolchain
.Nd compile CUDA source to PTX with clang and the cuda-native SDK tree
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm sh
.Pa lib/cuda-native/mksdk.sh
.Ar outdir
.Pp
.Nm clang++
.Fl x Cm cuda
.Fl -cuda-path Ns = Ns Ar outdir
.Fl -cuda-gpu-arch Ns = Ns Ar arch
.Fl -cuda-device-only
.Fl S
.Ar file.cu
.Sh DESCRIPTION
cuda-native is a CUDA stack for
.Fx
that uses no NVIDIA proprietary file.
This page describes its first piece: the SDK tree that clang takes as a CUDA
installation.
The tree holds headers written from the public CUDA API references and from
what clang's own CUDA runtime wrapper includes by name.
It does not hold a single file of NVIDIA's CUDA toolkit.
.Pp
.Pa mksdk.sh
assembles the tree in
.Ar outdir ,
which must be new or empty:
.Bl -tag -width "nvvm/libdevice/libdevice.10.bc"
.It Pa include/
the SDK headers;
.Pa cuda.h
sets
.Dv CUDA_VERSION
to 13000, and clang takes the SDK version from it.
.It Pa bin/
empty for now.
clang needs the directory to accept the tree as an installation.
.It Pa nvvm/libdevice/libdevice.10.bc
the device library that clang links into every device compile.
.It Pa version.json
cuda-native's own name and version, generated from the
.Dv CUDA_VERSION
and
.Dv CUDA_NATIVE_VERSION
macros of
.Pa cuda.h .
clang does not read it.
.El
.Pp
The compiler is clang from LLVM 23
.Pq the ports Pa llvm23 No package .
The base system clang is not used.
The tested
.Ar arch
values are
.Cm sm_120
.Pq compute capability 12.0, GeForce RTX 50 series such as the GB206 ,
.Cm sm_121
.Pq compute capability 12.1, DGX Spark GB10 ,
and their architecture-specific forms
.Cm sm_120a
and
.Cm sm_121a .
The output is PTX ISA 9.x text.
Other arch values that clang knows, such as
.Cm sm_120f
and
.Cm sm_121f ,
are not refused, but they are not tested.
.Pp
With
.Fl -cuda-host-only Fl c
clang builds the host object.
It leaves the launch calls
.Pq Fn cudaLaunchKernel , Fn __cudaPushCallConfiguration , Fn __cudaPopCallConfiguration
for the runtime library to provide.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width LLVM
.It Ev LLVM
The LLVM install that
.Pa mksdk.sh
and the test use; its clang must be version 23 or later.
The default is
.Pa /usr/local/llvm23 .
.It Ev TMPDIR
Where the test makes its scratch directory; the default is
.Pa /tmp .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "tests/cuda_native_toolchain_test.sh" -compact
.It Pa lib/cuda-native/sdk/
the sources of the tree
.It Pa lib/cuda-native/libdevice/libdevice.ll
the device library source
.It Pa lib/cuda-native/mksdk.sh
the assembler of the tree
.It Pa tests/cuda_native_toolchain_test.sh
the test: the tree, PTX for all four arches, the host object, provenance and
mutants
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Pa mksdk.sh
exits 0 when the tree is built, 2 when the arguments or
.Ar outdir
are refused, the LLVM tools are missing or older than 23, and 1 when a step fails.
A failed run leaves
.Ar outdir
as it was: the tree is built next to it and renamed into place at the end.
.Pp
The test exits with the number of failed checks, 77 when LLVM 23 is missing
(the checks that need it are skipped), and 99 when it cannot set up.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Build the tree and emit PTX for the GB10:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sh lib/cuda-native/mksdk.sh obj/cuda-native
/usr/local/llvm23/bin/clang++ -x cuda --cuda-path=obj/cuda-native \e
    --cuda-gpu-arch=sm_121 --cuda-device-only -S -o vadd.ptx vadd.cu
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clang 1
.Sh HISTORY
The SDK tree first appeared in the native CUDA work on Track #2380, stage C1.1
.Pq Track #2425 .
.Sh CAVEATS
The following pieces are missing:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
The device library has no functions yet.
A kernel that calls a math function such as
.Fn sinf
leaves an unresolved
.Li __nv_*
symbol in its PTX.
A later release adds a device library built from libclc.
.It
There is no
.Nm ptxas
and no
.Nm fatbinary
in
.Pa bin/ ,
so a full compile and link
.Pq without Fl -cuda-device-only No or Fl -cuda-host-only
does not work yet.
.It
There is no
.Nm libcudart
and no
.Nm libcuda
yet.
.El
.Pp
The headers declare only what clang's wrapper and the test kernels need.
.Fn atomicAdd
lowers to a system-scope atomic.
That is stronger than the device scope CUDA defines, so the results are
correct but it may be slower; a later release changes it.
